# Parallel Agent Coordination

## Branch Strategy

When working as one of multiple agents:
- Always work on dedicated feature branch
- Never commit directly to main/master
- Use naming: `feature/[task-name]` or `agent-[n]/[task-name]`

## Isolation Rules

- Assume other agents may modify shared files
- Pull latest before starting work
- Commit frequently with clear messages
- Resolve conflicts immediately if detected

## Communication via Git

- Use commit messages to document decisions
- Create PR descriptions that explain approach
- Reference related PRs if dependent work

## Handoff Format

When completing a task for another agent to review:
```
## Summary
[What was implemented]

## Changes
- file1.ts: [change description]
- file2.ts: [change description]

## Testing
[How to verify]

## Next Steps
[What remains or depends on this]
```

## Conflict Prevention

- Claim files at start of task (via commit/comment)
- Prefer additive changes over modifications
- Coordinate on shared config files
- Use feature flags for partial implementations
